WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.190
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm breaking down the new Incredibles

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:09.080
2 trailer for Pixar easter eggs, things you
might have missed, plus a theory about the

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.130
villain reveal.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:14.030
I'm also starting a giveaway for an awesome
Incredibles 2 Funko Pop.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:17.490
You just need to be a subscriber and leave
me a comment about the movie for a chance

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:18.490
to win.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:23.349
I'm going to start with the meeting at the
Devtech building where Mr Incredible, Elastigirl

00:00:23.349 --> 00:00:26.140
and Frozone are being introduced to Winston
Deavor.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:31.119
Remember in the sneak peek that Frozone mentioned
he'd been approached to set up just such a

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:32.119
meeting.

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:33.289
"I was approached by this tycoon."

00:00:33.289 --> 00:00:35.790
"Wants to talk ... about hero stuff."

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:41.129
Notice that in this scene, Mr Incredible and
Elastigirl are actually wearing their original

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:46.120
early costumes from the first movie before
Edna Mode made them the iconic red suits we're

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.170
more used to seeing them in.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:52.420
And notice that when Winston Deavor pitches
his idea to bring the Supers back into public

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:56.829
favour, he's showing a picture of the Incredibles
family being led away by a police officer.

00:00:56.829 --> 00:01:01.109
From the backdrop of the picture, it looks
like it might be during the aftermath of the

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:02.600
Underminer's rampage.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.680
There seems to be a lot of public damage and
destruction that happens during the Incredibles'

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:11.690
fight with the Underminer, and it sounds like
public opinion might be quite anti-Supers

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.960
even if the Parr family did succeed in taking
down the villain.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.760
There are also some very cool action shots
in the new trailer and I want to particularly

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.580
examine this shot of Dash.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:24.790
The young speedster is running through portals
that take him through solid objects.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:29.150
I think this could be the work of a new character
called Voyd who, according to the official

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:33.800
description for her character, has "the ability
to divert and manipulate objects around her

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:37.360
by creating voids that allow the objects to
appear and disappear."

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.910
Voyd hasn't shown up yet in the trailers,
but her character description also states

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.070
she's "a 'wannabe' Super and a mega-fan of
Elastigirl."

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:49.420
But what's also interesting in this scene
is that Dash appears to be running in a never-ending

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:50.420
loop.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.530
You can see an image of Dash running through
the same portal over and over in the distance.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:59.060
Now, judging by Voyd's character description,
it sounds like she'd be friendly to our band

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:03.952
of superheroes, but what if she's actually
a villain in disguise, masquerading as a fan

00:02:03.952 --> 00:02:05.730
of Elastigirl?

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.590
Could she have trapped Dash in an endless
loop of sorts?

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:12.410
Or maybe she is really on their side and created
this loop accidentally.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:17.750
A possible alternative is that these portals
are being created by Jack-Jack who has a ton

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:18.750
of superpowers.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:23.200
In fact, we've already seen him teleport himself
before now, including in another scene in

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.000
this trailer.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.790
And I wonder, if like me, those scenes made
you think a bit of the mutant Blink in X-Men:

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:33.010
Days of Future Past and also Vibe in TV's
The Flash.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:38.160
It also looks like Violet is getting some
new powers in the sequel to go with her adolescent

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.160
angst.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:42.490
As well as being able to create forcefield
energy shields that can protect her family,

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:47.130
there's a moment during what looks like the
Underminer sequence where she seems to cast

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:52.490
force blades or blasts that take out a piece
of falling rubble saving the people below.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:55.850
OK, let's get to the big villain reveal from
the trailer.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:03:01.750
"The Screenslaver interrupts this program
for an important announcement."

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:08.060
It looks like his dastardly plan will be hypnotising
and mind-controlling people via their TV screens.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:12.340
Elastigirl already seems to be aware of his
plan as notice how she's shielding her eyes

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:14.130
from the screens in the background here.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:18.150
This is happening at the local TV station
and I think this is going to tie in with the

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:22.060
scene earlier in the trailer where Elastigirl
attacks an escaping helicopter.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:28.170
A recent Incredibles 2 LEGO set has an "Elastigirl
Rooftop Pursuit" scene which shows that Screenslaver

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:32.870
is indeed the person piloting the helicopter
which also has a spinning hypno-propeller

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:35.170
that can hypnotise you if you look at it.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:39.470
And there's some evidence now which I think
ties Screenslaver with the head of the Devtech

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:40.980
corporation Winston Deavor.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:45.200
Firstly, the shape of Screenslaver's head
seems to match that of Winston's.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.670
And, secondly, think about what business Devtech
is involved in: It's a telecommunications

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:51.670
company.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:56.260
In fact, the LEGO set mentions that Screenslaver
is trying to hack into a satellite dish on

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:57.890
the roof of a building.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:02.360
And that LEGO set building is likely the same
TV building as in the trailer.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:06.940
On top of that, Winston has a sister called
Evelyn, who is the tech brainchild behind

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:08.220
the business.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:12.190
What's more as I mentioned in my breakdown
of the Olympics trailer, Evelyn Deavor could

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:17.010
be pronounced "Evil Endeavour", even if that's
a little on the nose, all of which gives me

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:19.979
the impression that these two could be up
to no good.

00:04:19.979 --> 00:04:24.800
There's also something fishy about the tycoon's
plan to recruit Elastigirl and there's a possible

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.449
hint at that in the recent Edna Mode teaser.

00:04:27.449 --> 00:04:30.139
"I'm not all dark and angsty."

00:04:30.139 --> 00:04:31.470
"I'm Elastigirl."

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.470
"Edna designed this?"

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:34.470
"No!

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.249
Some guy named Alexander Galbachy."

00:04:36.249 --> 00:04:41.490
I'm not sure if all these evil hints and links
to Devtech feel a little too obvious so perhaps

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:45.560
there'll be a further twist in the movie a
bit like we got with Coco, but at the moment,

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:48.309
I'm definitely getting some dodgy vibes from
Winston.

00:04:48.309 --> 00:04:52.889
By the way, it looks like this scene is happening
in the city of New Urbem as you can spot part

00:04:52.889 --> 00:04:56.159
of a sign for a "New Urbem Savings &amp; Loan"
bank in the distance.

00:04:56.159 --> 00:05:00.259
New Urbem is a new location that will be introduced
in Incredibles 2.

00:05:00.259 --> 00:05:04.080
There are also some Pixar easter eggs and
call backs in the trailer which I want to

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.080
talk about.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:06.080
"What!"

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.580
"Is this all vegetables?!"

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:10.499
"Who ordered all the vegetables?!"

00:05:10.499 --> 00:05:11.499
"I did."

00:05:11.499 --> 00:05:14.310
The shot of a mountain of broccoli on Dash's
plate as he complains about his mum ordering

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:19.979
a vegetable takeout dish is a hat-tip to Inside
Out and Riley's aversion to eating that particular

00:05:19.979 --> 00:05:20.979
vegetable.

00:05:20.979 --> 00:05:22.259
"Hold on, guys."

00:05:22.259 --> 00:05:23.400
"It's broccoli!"

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.400
"Yucky!"

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.389
"Well, I just saved our lives."

00:05:27.389 --> 00:05:28.389
"Yeah.

00:05:28.389 --> 00:05:29.389
You're welcome."

00:05:29.389 --> 00:05:33.539
And those Chinese takeout containers are also
another Pixar easter egg as the same style

00:05:33.539 --> 00:05:37.189
of food box has been used a number of times
in other Pixar movies.

00:05:37.189 --> 00:05:41.909
The first time was in A Bug's Life where it
was called the "Chinese Cabinet of Metamorphosis".

00:05:41.909 --> 00:05:46.639
It's also appeared in the Pizza Planet Truck
in Toy Story 2, in Linguini's apartment in

00:05:46.639 --> 00:05:50.909
Ratatouille, and it was also in Inside out
where, just like the Parr family, Riley and

00:05:50.909 --> 00:05:53.780
the Andersens sat down for a dinner of Chinese
takeout.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:59.280
One of the most memorable moments in the first
movie was when Frozone went to get his supersuit

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:03.520
so he could join the fight against Syndrome
and then this happened.

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:04.560
"Honey?"

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.629
"HONEY: What?

00:06:06.629 --> 00:06:09.289
"Where is my supersuit?"

00:06:09.289 --> 00:06:10.490
"HONEY: What?"

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:12.889
"Where is my supersuit?"

00:06:12.889 --> 00:06:16.479
"HONEY: I put it away.2
"Where?"

00:06:16.479 --> 00:06:18.249
"HONEY: Why do you need to know?"

00:06:18.249 --> 00:06:19.249
"I need it!"

00:06:19.249 --> 00:06:21.069
"HONEY: Don't you think about running off
doing no derrin'-do."

00:06:21.069 --> 00:06:22.499
"We are talking about the greater good."

00:06:22.499 --> 00:06:23.499
"HONEY: 'Greater good'?

00:06:23.499 --> 00:06:27.280
I am your wife!"

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.169
"I'm the greatest good you are ever gonna
get!"

00:06:30.169 --> 00:06:34.849
So, it was just fantastic to discover that
this time he's got his suit at the ready;

00:06:34.849 --> 00:06:39.990
although, by the sound of it, his wife Honey
still isn't overly keen on her husband's superhero

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:40.990
shenanigans.

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:42.990
"Suit up, it might get weird!"

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:44.710
"I'll be there, asap!"

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.280
"HONEY: Where you going asap?!

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.050
You better be back asap!"

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:51.279
Now, what do you think about the new Incredibles
2 trailer?

